      },
      "text": "Kernel methods provide a rigorous framework for learning in infinite-dimensional function spaces while keeping computation tractable via the kernel trick. The RKHS is the function-analytic foundation; SVMs are the canonical application; and the kernel trick reappears in the Neural Tangent Kernel (Module 06)."
    },
    {
      "id": "05-KERNEL-METHODS.md#003",
      "path": [
        "05-KERNEL-METHODS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:machine-learning-theory:05-kernel-methods, git-history:machine-learning-theory:05-kernel-methods]",
